    "parityApplicable": true,
    "knownNamespaceRoutes": [
      "GET /api/mcp/install-info"
    ],
    "reason": "CLI vs HTTP determination (C0-10, confirmed live): \"od mcp install <agent> --print\" (apps/daemon/src/cli.ts resolveMcpLaunchSpec) calls GET /api/mcp/install-info (this row declared endpoint, confirmed the correct and only HTTP call it makes) to get this daemon instance raw launch descriptor ({command,args,env,...}), then performs a LOCAL filesystem read of the target agent own existing MCP config file (e.g. ~/.cursor/mcp.json) and merges the two into a higher-level \"preview\" of the full file it would write. This is legitimate, architecturally necessary reshaping -- a stateless HTTP endpoint cannot see or replicate the caller local config file, so the CLI richer output is not the daemon dropping data, it is the CLI adding data the daemon structurally cannot have. The divergence is total at the top level (CLI: ok/agent/kind/configPath/preview/message; HTTP: command/args/env/daemonUrl/webBaseUrl/platform/cliExists/nodeExists/buildHint -- zero shared keys), and the genuinely-comparable fields (command/args/env) are only reachable by parsing a JSON string nested inside the CLI own \"preview\" field, which none of the four supported valueComparison modes (exact/unordered-array/composite/binary) can express -- composite in particular requires every declared field to be present in BOTH payloads, and none are. No valueComparison is declared: this row is left at the strict default (which will legitimately fail if sample-selected) and reported here as a real, understood gate-comparator-vocabulary gap rather than forced with an inapplicable mode."
  },
